<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Go to Him “without the camp,”</l><l>Willing e’en to bear the cross;</l><l>He has trod the narrow way,</l><l>I will follow, suff’ring loss.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Go to Him “without the camp,”</l><l>Dear ones, relatives forsake;</l><l>He the Father’s will did mind,</l><l>In His passion I partake.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Go to Him “without the camp,”</l><l>His companion I will be;</l><l>Never join religion’s ranks</l><l>Or the world’s society.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Go to Him “without the camp,”</l><l>Though the path be lone and grim;</l><l>Let all human friends desert,</l><l>I am satisfied with Him.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>Go to Him “without the camp,”</l><l>There to walk with Him, how blest!</l><l>E’er to see His smiling face</l><l>Ever in His presence rest.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>Go to Him “without the camp,”</l><l>Till the dawning of the day;</l><l>Then I’ll see Him and rejoice,</l><l>With Him in His kingdom stay.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
